				<r3d:description language="eng">The Shuttle Radar Topography Mission, which flew aboard NASA&#039;s Space Shuttle Endeavour during an 11-day mission in 2000, made the first near-global topographical map of Earth, collecting data on nearly 80 percent of Earth&#039;s land surfaces. 

 The instrument&#039;s design was essentially a modified version of the earlier Shuttle Imaging Radar instruments with a second antenna added to allow for topographic mapping using a technique similar to stereo photography.</r3d:description>
